# A Functorial Bridge from Species Generating Functions to Tropical Valuation Profiles

Bridge: connects `Applications/CombinatorialSpecies` (exponential generating functions and
the binomial/Day-convolution product of species) to the tropical / min-plus world of
`Bridges/CategoricalTropicalUltrametric` and the non-archimedean valuation themes of
`Computation/PadicValuationDepth`.

## The mathematical message

Apply a (Krull) **additive valuation** `v : K → WithTop ℤ` coefficient-wise to a counting
sequence `a : ℕ → K`.  The result `vprofile V a : ℕ → WithTop ℤ` is the **tropical valuation
profile** of the species/GF.  The classical EGF dictionary

  sum of species          ↔ sum of EGFs
  product of species (`binConv`) ↔ Cauchy/binomial product of EGFs

*tropicalizes* to a **lax functor** into the min-plus semiring `(WithTop ℤ, min, +)`:

* **Sum law (tropical).**  `min (vprofile V a) (vprofile V b) ≤ vprofile V (a + b)`
  — the ultrametric inequality, applied coefficient-wise.
* **Product law (tropical).**  `tropConv (vprofile V a) (vprofile V b) ≤ vprofile V (binConv a b)`
  where `tropConv u w n = inf_{i+j=n} (u i + w j)` is the **min-plus (tropical) convolution**.
  This is the tropical shadow of `egf_mul`: the Cauchy product of generating functions degrades
  to the inf-convolution of valuation profiles (a Newton-polygon lower bound).

The inequalities are *lax* (≤, not =): valuations only see a lower bound on coefficients,
because of cancellation and because the binomial coefficients `C(n,i)` carry non-negative
valuation.  This is exactly the tropicalization phenomenon — equality holds generically
(at "tropically transverse" supports) but the functor is laxly monoidal in general.

## Main results
* `AddVal.v_natCast_nonneg`     — natural-number coefficients have non-negative valuation.
* `AddVal.v_sum_ge`             — the finite ultrametric inequality: `inf v(fᵢ) ≤ v(∑ fᵢ)`.
* `vprofile_add_ge`             — tropical sum law (coefficient-wise ultrametric).
* `vprofile_binConv_ge`         — tropical product law: min-plus convolution lower-bounds the
                                  profile of the binomial convolution.
* `vprofile_const_one`          — the species of sets has the constant-`0` (tropical unit) profile.
* `padicAddVal`                 — the `p`-adic valuation as an `AddVal ℚ`, tying the bridge to
                                  `PadicValuationDepth`.
-/
import Mathlib

open scoped BigOperators
open Finset

namespace SpeciesTropicalValuation

noncomputable section

/-! ## §0. The binomial (exponential) convolution

This reproduces `CombinatorialSpecies.binConv` from `Applications/CombinatorialSpecies.lean`
(the counting law of the structural/Day-convolution product of species, whose EGF is the
*product* of the EGFs by `egf_mul`).  We keep a local copy so this bridge file is
self-contained; the two definitions are definitionally identical:
`(a ⋆ b)ₙ = ∑_{i+j=n} C(n,i)·aᵢ·bⱼ`. -/

/-- The binomial (exponential) convolution of two counting sequences, matching
`CombinatorialSpecies.binConv`. -/
def binConv (a b : ℕ → ℚ) : ℕ → ℚ :=
  fun n => ∑ p ∈ Finset.antidiagonal n, (n.choose p.1 : ℚ) * a p.1 * b p.2

/-! ## §1. Additive (Krull) valuations with values in `WithTop ℤ` -/

/-- An **additive (Krull) valuation** on a field `K` with values in `WithTop ℤ`.
`v 0 = ⊤` (the tropical zero / `+∞`), `v` is multiplicative (turning products into sums), and
satisfies the **ultrametric** inequality `min (v x) (v y) ≤ v (x + y)`. -/
structure AddVal (K : Type*) [Field K] where
  /-- The underlying valuation map. -/
  v : K → WithTop ℤ
  v_zero : v 0 = ⊤
  v_one : v 1 = 0
  v_mul : ∀ x y, v (x * y) = v x + v y
  v_add_ge : ∀ x y, min (v x) (v y) ≤ v (x + y)

namespace AddVal

variable {K : Type*} [Field K] (V : AddVal K)

/-- Natural-number coefficients have non-negative valuation: `0 ≤ v (n : K)`.
(`v 1 = 0`, and the ultrametric inequality keeps `v (1 + … + 1) ≥ 0`.) -/
lemma v_natCast_nonneg (n : ℕ) : 0 ≤ V.v (n : K) := by
  induction' n with n ih;
  · simp +decide [ V.v_zero ];
  · convert V.v_add_ge n 1 |> le_trans _ using 1;
    · norm_cast;
    · exact le_min ih ( by rw [ V.v_one ] )

/-- **Finite ultrametric inequality.**  The valuation of a finite sum is at least the infimum
of the valuations of the summands: `inf_{i∈s} v(fᵢ) ≤ v(∑_{i∈s} fᵢ)`. -/
lemma v_sum_ge {ι : Type*} (s : Finset ι) (f : ι → K) :
    s.inf (fun i => V.v (f i)) ≤ V.v (∑ i ∈ s, f i) := by
      induction' s using Finset.induction with i s hi ih;
      all_goals try exact Classical.decEq _;
      · simp +decide [ V.v_zero ];
      · have := V.v_add_ge ( f i ) ( ∑ i ∈ s, f i );
        simp_all +decide [ Finset.inf_insert ];
        exact Or.imp id ( fun h => le_trans ih h ) this

end AddVal

/-! ## §2. Tropical valuation profiles and min-plus operations -/

variable {K : Type*} [Field K]

/-- The **tropical valuation profile** of a counting sequence: apply the valuation
coefficient-wise. -/
def vprofile (V : AddVal K) (a : ℕ → K) : ℕ → WithTop ℤ := fun n => V.v (a n)

/-- The **tropical (min-plus) addition** of two profiles: coefficient-wise `min`. -/
def tropMin (u w : ℕ → WithTop ℤ) : ℕ → WithTop ℤ := fun n => min (u n) (w n)

/-- The **tropical (min-plus) convolution** of two profiles:
`(u ⊛ w) n = inf_{i+j=n} (u i + w j)`. This is the tropical shadow of the Cauchy product. -/
def tropConv (u w : ℕ → WithTop ℤ) : ℕ → WithTop ℤ :=
  fun n => (antidiagonal n).inf (fun p => u p.1 + w p.2)

@[simp] lemma vprofile_apply (V : AddVal K) (a : ℕ → K) (n : ℕ) :
    vprofile V a n = V.v (a n) := rfl

/-! ## §3. The bridge theorems -/

/-- **Tropical sum law.**  The profile of a coefficient-wise sum dominates the `min` of the
profiles: the ultrametric inequality, said tropically.  This is the tropicalization of
`egf_add`. -/
theorem vprofile_add_ge (V : AddVal K) (a b : ℕ → K) (n : ℕ) :
    tropMin (vprofile V a) (vprofile V b) n ≤ vprofile V (fun n => a n + b n) n := by
  exact V.v_add_ge _ _

/-- **Tropical product law (the bridge).**  The profile of the binomial convolution `binConv`
(the counting law of the species product, whose EGF is the *product* of EGFs by `egf_mul`)
dominates the **min-plus convolution** of the profiles.  This is the lax-monoidal tropicalization
of `egf_mul`: the Cauchy product of generating functions becomes the inf-convolution of
valuation profiles — a Newton-polygon lower bound. -/
theorem vprofile_binConv_ge (V : AddVal ℚ) (a b : ℕ → ℚ) (n : ℕ) :
    tropConv (vprofile V a) (vprofile V b) n ≤ vprofile V (binConv a b) n := by
  refine' le_trans _ ( V.v_sum_ge _ _ );
  refine' Finset.le_inf _ ; simp_all +decide [ tropConv, vprofile ];
  intro i j hij; rw [ ← hij ] ; simp +decide [ V.v_mul ] ;
  refine' le_trans ( Finset.inf_le ( show ( i, j ) ∈ antidiagonal ( i + j ) from _ ) ) _ <;> norm_num [ add_assoc ];
  exact le_add_of_nonneg_left ( by exact_mod_cast V.v_natCast_nonneg _ )

/-- The **species of sets** `E` (constant-one counting sequence) has the constant-`0` profile —
the tropical multiplicative unit.  (Tropical shadow of `egf_const_one : EGF E = exp`.) -/
@[simp] theorem vprofile_const_one (V : AddVal K) (n : ℕ) :
    vprofile V (fun _ => (1 : K)) n = 0 := by
  simp [vprofile, V.v_one]

/-! ## §4. The `p`-adic instantiation — tie-in to `PadicValuationDepth` -/

/-- The `p`-adic valuation map on `ℚ` with values in `WithTop ℤ`, using the convention
`v 0 = ⊤`. -/
def padicValWithTop (p : ℕ) (x : ℚ) : WithTop ℤ :=
  if x = 0 then (⊤ : WithTop ℤ) else (padicValRat p x : WithTop ℤ)

@[simp] lemma padicValWithTop_zero (p : ℕ) : padicValWithTop p 0 = ⊤ := by
  simp [padicValWithTop]

lemma padicValWithTop_one (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] : padicValWithTop p 1 = 0 := by
  -- By definition, `padicValWithTop p 1 = 0` because `1` is not zero and its `p`-adic valuation is `0`.
  simp [padicValWithTop]

lemma padicValWithTop_mul (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (x y : ℚ) :
    padicValWithTop p (x * y) = padicValWithTop p x + padicValWithTop p y := by
  by_cases hx : x = 0 <;> by_cases hy : y = 0 <;> simp +decide [ *, padicValWithTop ] at *;
  rw_mod_cast [ padicValRat.mul hx hy ]

lemma padicValWithTop_add_ge (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (x y : ℚ) :
    min (padicValWithTop p x) (padicValWithTop p y) ≤ padicValWithTop p (x + y) := by
  by_cases hx : x = 0 <;> by_cases hy : y = 0 <;> simp +decide [ *, padicValWithTop ] at *;
  split_ifs <;> simp_all +decide [ add_eq_zero_iff_eq_neg ];
  have := @padicValRat.min_le_padicValRat_add p;
  exact min_le_iff.mp ( this ( add_eq_zero_iff_eq_neg.not.mpr ‹_› ) )

/-- The `p`-adic valuation packaged as an `AddVal ℚ`, with the convention `v 0 = ⊤`.
This makes the abstract tropical bridge concrete and non-archimedean, linking the species GF
world to `Computation/PadicValuationDepth`. -/
def padicAddVal (p : ℕ) [hp : Fact p.Prime] : AddVal ℚ where
  v := padicValWithTop p
  v_zero := padicValWithTop_zero p
  v_one := padicValWithTop_one p
  v_mul := padicValWithTop_mul p
  v_add_ge := padicValWithTop_add_ge p

